    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2AuTBzJ27DP6jfunJgWsvcA)_\n\nExtends `sp-org-issues-morning` with two sections, both read through `gh api` (REST, no GraphQL):\n\n- **Notes to self**: your comments (conversation and review comments) on an open PR that start with `Note to self:`, each linking to the comment. These are reminders for you; Claude does not act on or reply to them.\n- **Needs further testing**: PRs labelled `needs-further-testing`, open or already merged (the label means merged into main for faster testing, not fully tested yet). Not ranked.\n\nEmpty sections are left out. Settings: `sp-org-issues-morning-self`, `sp-org-issues-morning-testing-label`.\n\nWritten test first (commit 1 is the failing tests, commit 2 the code). The test header now also stubs `sp-yadm-repo`, `sp-src-dir`, `sp-clones-dir` and `sp-path`, because the suite no longer loaded headless since `sp-org-issues-repos` started using them.\n\n**Tested**: 32 ERT tests pass headless (Emacs 29.3): parsing, filtering, rendering, and the fetch against a fake `gh api`. The parsers were also run on live REST answers for this repository (29 labelled PRs parsed; there were no matching notes yet).\n**Not tested**: the `*Morning*` buffer end to end with the real `gh` on your Mac.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBCpJA5AHLRCRXXsj4)_",
